    id: 'kit-08-fenwick-tree', n: 8, week: 2, title: 'Fenwick tree', timebox: '45 minutes',
    brief: `A **Fenwick tree** (binary indexed tree) supports point updates and prefix sums in O(log n) each, using one array and the lowest-set-bit trick \`i & -i\`.

- \`add(index, delta)\` adds \`delta\` to the element at \`index\` (0-based; all elements start at 0).
- \`prefixSum(index)\` returns the sum of elements \`0 … index\`; \`rangeSum(l, r)\` returns the inclusive sum.

Store the tree 1-indexed internally. It’s a classic source of off-by-one bugs.`,
